  "id": "murphy-shakti8-feelgood-1phase-frontal",
  "name": "8 Coil Shakti Feelgood: one phase, frontal",
  "category": "mood",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "fidelity": "approximation",
  "dose": {"value": [10, 50], "unit": "mG", "plane": "unstated", "cite": "Murphy, measurement.htm"},
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti); signal templates licensed from Persinger & Koren",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's one-phase Feelgood session for the 8 Coil Shakti: the amygdala and hippocampal signals one after the other with 4-s pauses, over both frontal lobes only. The vendor calls it 'the most effective feelgood session' and says to begin with it rather than the two-phase version.",
  "notes": "The vendor's Feelgood session plays the signals over the temporal lobes, then the frontal lobes, for '20 or 30 minutes' each (shakti_happiness.htm); the one-phase form is 'doing only the second phase, which applies the signals only to the frontal lobes'. The demo video: 'choose 20 minutes that's usually a fine length for most people' (captions at 4:52). Phase 1 (20 min) is the 20-min version: stop after it, or let phase 2 (10 min) run for the 30-min version. Four coils on CH5-8 (Fp1, AF3, Fp2, AF4) carry the signal together. Sites and polarity are this project's reading of vendor photos: AF3 and Fp2 are reversed. One pass: amygdala signal, 4 s of silence, hippocampal signal, 4 s of silence. Both are rebuilt: the vendor's files are not published. The amygdala signal is the project's rising sweep (6 to 30 Hz) with the published point duration and length (230 points of 3 ms; Ryczko 2002 p.1 [592]); its point values were never published as numbers, only as a small figure. The hippocampal signal is a primed burst on 1-ms points: one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]). The vendor says 'the standard signals have 3 msec points' (rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm), so the point duration is this project's choice. The vendor's 10 to 50 mG carries no distance (measurement.htm, duds.htm); an independent meter read 0.1 to 1.0 uT RMS about 9 cm from the coils (Gendle 2012 p.11 [227]). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. The effects are vendor claims. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). You may feel 'a bit foggy' right after (vendor). Too many frontal or temporal sessions 'can create a kind of malaise or even lethargy' (vendor). Not a treatment for depression or any illness. Not for people with a psychiatric diagnosis or epilepsy; stop if distressed.",
  "setting": "Not in sensory deprivation: the vendor says the Feelgood session 'should not be done in sensory deprivation', since it is meant for 'outward-looking', 'this-worldly' effects. No time of day is prescribed (the vendor's page on weekly sessions says they 'can be done any time of day'); the vendor notes that the effect often shows only the morning after.",
  "schedule": "Vendor: 6 weekly sessions or 6 sessions every 3 days (never more often than every 72 h), then 3 weeks off. If a session is interrupted before it ends, wait three days and start it again from the beginning (if you miss a session of an every-3-days series, the vendor says to stop for three weeks).",
  "targets": ["vmpfc", "left-dlpfc", "right-dlpfc"],
